+# PocketRisu host change stream C0 validation
+
+Date: 2026-09-13 KST
+
+Status: **ordered-ingest and source-invalidation store primitives validated;
+Node durability and product transport remain unimplemented**
+
+## Scope and authority
+
+This is the C0-C experiment for the PocketRisu server chat-save integration
+plan. It starts from Archive Center `026dcbf3b45adcf69b254673d439b24e943115b3`
+and records implementation commits `17fcdd1`, `d063b68`, and `6866ccd`. It adds
+only:
+
+- additive MariaDB per-binding host-change streams and immutable event receipts;
+- an optional MariaDB store interface for contiguous ingest, stream status, and
+  mutation-source invalidation;
+- execution acquire integration with the exact binding stream watermark;
+- reuse of the existing source lifecycle, derived cleanup, vector outbox, and
+  canonical-tail exclusion owners; and
+- SQL-mock, source-shape, and explicitly disposable MariaDB tests.
+
+No HTTP route, host authentication, capability advertisement, Archive Center
+JavaScript change, PocketRisu durable intent writer, provider call, or patched
+runtime installation is part of this slice.
+
+## Runtime audit Phase 1 — flat discovery
+
+- Migration 015 creates one stream per exact host instance, character, chat,
+  and binding epoch.
+- Each stream stores independent contiguous `ingested_seq` and `safe_seq`
+  watermarks.
+- Migration 015 creates immutable event receipts unique by both event ID and
+  sequence within a stream.
+- Event receipts separate ingest state from source-safety state and retain the
+  first host commit time and immutable payload reference.
+- The stream key is a SHA-256 digest, while the full normalized identity is
+  retained and checked after lookup.
+- Intent validation bounds identifier bytes, message-identity count, encoded
+  identity bytes, and supported event kinds.
+- Intent validation rejects control characters, duplicate message identities,
+  zero or non-forward sequence numbers, missing commit time, and invalid
+  revision transitions.
+- Ingest locks the current route and stream in a serializable MariaDB
+  transaction.
+- Ingest returns an exact stored receipt for the same event fingerprint even
+  after the route is removed or rebound.
+- Ingest rejects reuse of an event ID with different content and reuse of a
+  sequence with another event ID.
+- Ingest reports the first required sequence without writing an out-of-order
+  event.
+- Content-changing events enter `pending`; `ac_skip` and `operation_end` enter
+  `safe` only when their revisions are unchanged.
+- A safe no-source-change event cannot advance the stream watermark across an
+  earlier pending event.
+- Ingest updates a matching active execution slot's observed watermarks in the
+  same transaction.
+- Source invalidation accepts only stored `edit`, `delete`, `reroll`, or
+  `branch` events.
+- Source invalidation resolves the event's bounded message/source identities
+  against source revision history in the stream's canonical session.
+- A mutation whose source identity has not been observed remains pending and
+  does not advance `safe_seq`.
+- A matched mutation invalidates active source revisions from the earliest
+  matched turn through the current tail.
+- Source invalidation marks derivation dependencies and precise units stale,
+  rejects queued or leased critic/vector work, and enqueues known vector
+  deletes.
+- The same transaction excludes stale turn-range raw and derived Archive
+  Center projections with the existing canonical-tail cleanup owner.
+- The same transaction restores older still-active status projections after
+  removing the invalidated tail.
+- `safe_seq` advances only through a verified contiguous prefix of event rows
+  whose safety state is `safe`.
+- Applying the same already-safe mutation is idempotent and does not repeat
+  source cleanup or release another execution.
+- A matched source mutation records an immutable invalidated/deleted execution
+  outcome and releases the exact active slot in the same transaction.
+- A new acquire reads and locks the exact binding stream rather than inheriting
+  a scalar watermark from an older binding epoch.
+- Acquire waits when the exact stream's `safe_seq` is below the requested host
+  change boundary.
+- Store reconnection preserves receipts, watermarks, source lifecycle, worker
+  fences, and execution outcomes.
+- MariaDB deadlock and lock-timeout errors retry the complete normalized
+  transaction within a fixed bound.
+- The source-safety transaction holds the existing memory-derivation write
+  mutex and may perform turn-tail cleanup proportional to affected state.
+- Event and stream rows have no retention or compaction policy in this slice.
+- `payload_ref` is stored as an opaque identifier; this store slice cannot
+  prove that the referenced Node payload is immutable or exists.
+- `input_commit` and `response_commit` have no source-safety completion action
+  in this slice and therefore remain pending.
+- A source identity that is not yet present requires a later reconciliation
+  call; this slice does not install a background reconciler.
+- Multiple binding streams that resolve to one Archive Center session are not
+  aggregated into one claim request in this slice.
+- No HTTP handler or production caller invokes the optional host-change store
+  interface.
+- The tables contain identifiers, revisions, hashes, timestamps, and payload
+  references, but no raw chat or model text.
+- The code adds no goroutine, polling loop, socket, external lock service, or
+  Chroma call inside the MariaDB transaction.
+
+## Runtime audit Phase 2 — external anchors
+
+### Ordered schema, identity, and replay
+
+Type: structural and measured.
+
+Breaking scenarios: two events claim the same sequence, an ACK loss causes the
+same event to execute twice, an event is replayed with changed content, or a
+new binding epoch inherits an old stream's sequence. Migration 015 has unique
+`(stream_key,event_id)` and `(stream_key,seq)` keys. The stream digest includes
+the binding epoch, and every loaded stream is compared with the retained full
+identity. Ingest locks the route and stream, checks an existing immutable event
+before current-binding rejection, and requires both `seq == ingested+1` and
+`previousSeq == ingested` before insert.
+
+The disposable MariaDB test observed the required sequence for two separate
+gaps, exact receipt replay, changed-payload conflict, store close/reopen,
+concurrent sequence 3/4 convergence after gap retry, old-epoch rejection, old
+receipt replay, and a new epoch beginning at sequence 1.
+
+Anchors:
+
+- `migrations/015_host_change_stream.sql:7`
+- `migrations/015_host_change_stream.sql:24`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_host_change.go:130`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_host_change.go:313`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_host_change_integration_test.go:14`
+
+Failure behavior: validation happens before I/O. Every failed begin, select,
+insert, conditional update, row-count check, or commit returns an error and the
+transaction guard rolls back. Retry is limited to MariaDB 1205 and 1213.
+
+### Source identity and conservative safety admission
+
+Type: structural and measured.
+
+Breaking scenario: an edit names a message Archive Center has never accepted,
+but the server interprets absence as proof that no stale source exists. The
+source-safety action decodes and revalidates the stored identity set, locks
+matching source history, and returns `pending/source_target_not_observed` when
+no source row matches. It does not change the event or watermark in that path.
+
+When history matches, the earliest matching turn is the invalidation boundary.
+The action checks whether any active source remains at or after that boundary,
+uses the existing source invalidation owner when necessary, and records either
+the applied lifecycle disposition or `source_already_inactive`.
+
+Anchors:
+
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_host_change.go:153`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_host_change.go:777`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_host_change.go:838`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_host_change_test.go:247`
+
+### Read exclusion before safe watermark
+
+Type: structural and measured.
+
+Breaking scenario: `memory_source_revisions` becomes inactive but an aggregate
+`memories` row or raw `chat_logs` row remains visible to prepare. The first
+audit pass found that the existing lifecycle invalidator alone did not exclude
+those readers. The source-safety transaction now invokes the existing
+`canonicalTailDeleteCommands` owner with the matched positive turn and deletes
+the stale AC raw/derived tail before writing the event safety receipt. It then
+restores older active status projections. Negative-turn external imports are
+outside the `>= matched turn` range.
+
+The disposable test inserted a raw user/assistant pair and aggregate memory,
+applied the edit, and observed zero rows through both `ListChatLogs` and
+`ListMemories` before accepting the final `safe_seq=1` result.
+
+Anchors:
+
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_host_change.go:855`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_logical_turn_replace.go:177`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_logical_turn_replace.go:232`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_host_change_integration_test.go:203`
+
+Failure behavior: any source lifecycle write or read-exclusion delete failure
+returns before the safety receipt and rolls back the transaction. The focused
+failure test drives successful source-stale writes followed by a cleanup write
+failure and observes rollback with no result.
+
+### Worker and vector fences
+
+Type: structural and measured.
+
+Breaking scenario: a critic or vector worker leases work before an edit, then
+commits after the edit is declared safe. `invalidateMemorySourcesTx` locks the
+source revisions, rejects pending/leased/retryable reprocessing jobs and vector
+upserts, invalidates precise projections, and queues deletes for known vector
+documents before changing source lifecycle. Claim queries require an active
+source. Vector materialization completion locks both outbox and source state
+and rejects stale rows.
+
+The disposable test began with a live source, leased reprocessing job, and
+leased vector upsert. After restart and mutation apply it observed source
+`invalidated`, both workers `stale_rejected`, a late materialization result of
+`ErrSourceRevisionStale`, and no stale raw/aggregate readback.
+
+Anchors:
+
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_memory_derivation.go:501`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_memory_derivation.go:912`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_memory_derivation.go:1216`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_memory_derivation.go:1605`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_host_change_integration_test.go:203`
+
+Physical Chroma deletion remains asynchronous. Safety does not depend on that
+I/O completing: stale MariaDB projection rows are removed or lifecycle-filtered
+before `safe_seq` advances, and delete work is durable first.
+
+### Contiguous safety and execution ownership
+
+Type: structural and measured.
+
+Breaking scenarios: sequence 2 is safe while sequence 1 is pending and the
+watermark jumps to 2; an acquire for binding epoch B reads epoch A's scalar
+slot watermark; or an active generation writes after an edit. Safe-prefix
+calculation checks the expected row count and minimum/maximum sequence, then
+stops before the first non-safe row. Acquire locks the exact stream before the
+session slot and snapshots that stream's watermarks into the claim. Ingest
+updates a matching live claim. Mutation apply creates a deterministic terminal
+event, records an invalidated/deleted outcome, and clears only the exact claim
+epoch.
+
+The real test observed a safe operation-end event behind pending sequence 1
+without a watermark leap. The source-fence test then observed active
+`ingested=1/safe=0`, a durable invalidated outcome after restart, and a new
+operation acquiring only with `requiredHostChangeSeq=1` after `safe=1`.
+
+Anchors:
+
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_host_change.go:864`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_host_change.go:892`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_host_change.go:1021`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_host_change.go:1047`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_session_execution.go:204`
+- `go-service/internal/store/mariadb_session_execution.go:249`
+
+### Migration, reachability, resources, encoding, and security
+
+Type: structural, measured, and surfaced.
+
+The content-copy session migration manifest remains v4 and excludes
+`host_change_streams`; event rows are transitively owned by their stream. The
