+   - Review trigger: C4/C6 status DTO must expose or fence the joined terminal
+     disposition and test new-browser recovery.
+
+8. **Lock contention and multi-stream session policy**
+   - Resolved: observed register/start/ready-skip races converge, and 1205/1213
+     retries are bounded.
+   - Missing link: host-change source apply locks slot then prepare, while some
+     prepare transitions lock prepare then route/slot; multi-stream aggregation
+     is also absent.
+   - Limitation: unobserved high-contention frequency and cross-stream policy
+     cannot be inferred from source tests.
+   - Review trigger: C6 must run concurrent edit/ready/settle fault injection,
+     measure retries, and check all attached stream boundaries.
+
+9. **Patched process restart**
+   - Resolved: store reconnect recovers ready/running/unknown/skipped and the
+     ARM64 backend builds.
+   - Missing link: the running isolated 4.3.1 package remains unmodified and no
+     host route reaches the registry.
+   - Limitation: store reconnect is not end-to-end process recovery.
+   - Review trigger: after C4 mounts the route, repeat response loss and
+     process stop/start on the isolated stack before live integration.
+
+## Cross-piece interaction check
+
+- Migration plus store: production loader replay and real MariaDB transitions
+  use the same columns, checks, and indexes.
+- C0-B execution plus C0-D prepare: register/start bind the exact route,
+  operation, claim epoch, and source watermark; skip records a terminal outcome
+  and clears only that claim.
+- C0-C changes plus C0-D prepare: pending change blocks prepare; applied source
+  invalidation fences ready/running prepare rows before releasing execution.
+- Ready plus skip: the final registry tombstone contains no result bytes and
+  repeated skip preserves the release receipt.
+- Terminal execution plus stale skip: existing outcome wins and retained ready
+  bytes are not rewritten.
+- Restart plus unknown: persisted running state is observable, but only an
+  explicit recovery action can mark unknown; neither path grants start again.
+- Existing HTTP contracts: no prepare/complete handler or v1-v3 source
+  acceptance behavior changed, so this slice cannot be reached as product
+  support.
+- Session migration plus coordination: content manifest v4 remains unchanged
+  and registry rows are not copied as narrative content.
+
+## Verification
+
+- Thirty-five combined host-prepare/host-change/host-execution tests are
+  listed; seven are host-prepare-specific.
+- The three explicitly disposable MariaDB tests for execution, host change,
+  and prepare pass together.
+- The entire `internal/store` package passes.
+- The focused host-prepare/change/execution set passes under Go's race
+  detector.
+- The complete Go repository test suite and `go vet ./...` pass.
+- `node --check "Archive Center.js"` passes; JavaScript bytes are unchanged.
+- The final Linux arm64 build is 36,486,406 bytes with SHA-256
